{
  "note": "kakure_pool is a native solana-program crate, not an Anchor program (Anchor 1.1.2 fails to run on this container's glibc 2.35, and the only working local Anchor, 0.30.0, predates Agave 3.0; see the workstream-B final report). This file is therefore a hand-written IDL-equivalent, not a real Anchor IDL, published early per the task brief so the SDK team can code against final account/instruction shapes. Wire format is documented per-field below.",
  "programName": "kakure_pool",
  "encoding": {
    "instructions": "borsh::to_vec of the Rust `PoolInstruction` enum (programs/kakure_pool/src/instruction.rs): a single leading u8 variant tag equal to the variant's 0-based declaration order below, followed by the borsh encoding of its fields. This is NOT Anchor's 8-byte sighash discriminator.",
    "events": "sol_log_data(tag_bytes, borsh(event_struct)) -- one program-log line per event, NOT emit_cpi! (Anchor unavailable). tag_bytes is the ASCII string in each event's `tag` field below; borsh() has no leading discriminator.",
    "fields": "[u8;32] fields are big-endian 32-byte field elements unless noted; Pubkey fields are the raw 32-byte address.",
    "verifierCpi": "Internal to the program (not part of any instruction's own encoding): the CPI data sent to a verifier program is `proof_bytes ‖ 12-byte gnark witness header (nr_public_inputs, nr_private_inputs=0, entries_count, each big-endian u32) ‖ public_inputs (32 bytes each, big-endian, in order)` -- exactly gnark's own `.pw` serialization (see circuits/README.md), so a real Sunspot-built verifier binary can be dropped in unmodified."
  },
  "instructions": [
    {
      "tag": 0, "name": "initialize",
      "args": [
        { "name": "compliance_pk_x", "type": "[u8;32]" },
